status GREEN on the work, with two self-inflicted faults recorded above. Cold roster 205 guards, 176 green, 0 red, 2 gated (pond, expected), run_verdict=ok. docs_command_path, tracked_link, ascii_document, qa_report_card, living_docs_lint, exec_bit, reds_pin_capacity, reds_spine_derive and reds_ledger_monotone all GREEN after the change. Page re-graded A 94; shelf A+ 100. Written before the send.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the repair is landed and the class is measured at one firing, so no guard was built. The open question is whether this tree wants an instrument that reads a printed command for TERMINATION rather than reachability, since the only honest way to answer is to run it, and running a page's commands is exactly what no guard does today. Two of my instruments called a hanging command healthy this lap; that is either acceptable and named, or it is the next loom.
